<https://brickschema.org/schema/Brick#Velocity_Pressure> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Dynamic Pressure (indicated with q, or Q, and sometimes called velocity pressure) is the quantity defined by: (q = 1/2 * ρ v^{2}), where (using SI units),  (q) is dynamic pressure in (pascals), (ρ) is fluid density in (kg/m^{3}) (for example, density of air) and (v ) is fluid velocity in (m/s)."@en ;
